@@ -5,6 +5,21 @@
 
 ## 2026-08-30
 
+### 0809 — Managed LLDB Wrapper Health Uses Canonical Bytes And Delegation
+- ROOT CAUSE: `scripts/setup.sh` rewrote its wrapper every run and a line-presence check could accept unreachable delegation after an early `exit 0`.
+- FIX: One renderer owns the wrapper bytes; setup preserves a byte-identical executable and atomically repairs every divergent managed wrapper.
+- EVIDENCE: `TestBootstrapSetupRepairsManagedLLDBMCPWrapperWithUnreachableExpectedTarget` drives root `setup.sh`, then executes the repaired wrapper and observes helper argument delegation.
+
+### 0808 — LLDB Setup Installs LLVM Only When Required
+- ROOT CAUSE: `install_lldb_mcp` invoked `brew install llvm` unconditionally before validating the already-installed helper and adjacent `lldb`.
+- FIX: `scripts/setup.sh` probes `brew --prefix llvm` and both executables first; a second production setup neither invokes Homebrew install nor changes wrapper inode.
+- EVIDENCE: `TestBootstrapSetupInstallsLLDBMCPOnceAndWrapperDelegates` runs root `setup.sh` twice and records one install plus stable inode.
+
+### 0807 — LLDB MCP Bootstrap Now Fails Closed
+- REGRESSION: macOS setup without Homebrew or external `lldb-mcp` returned success and printed `=== Done ===`, leaving project opt-in unavailable.
+- FIX: `scripts/setup.sh` now returns non-zero with actionable remediation when Homebrew/prefix/install/helper/lldb prerequisites cannot be established.
+- EVIDENCE: `TestBootstrapSetupRefusesMissingLLDBMCPPrerequisites` and `TestBootstrapSetupRefusesLLVMInstallWithoutExpectedHelper` drive root `setup.sh` and require refusal before success output.
+
 ### 0646 — Correction: Readiness Test Predates Later Main State
 - CORRECTION: `TestPiLaunchReadinessServiceUnavailableStillHonorsRuntimeBoundsAtProductionEntry` was introduced in `97ebda4`, not after `TASK-260817-3a0zr3`; it passes in the exact `0413aee` task-head suite and fails only in the current-main runs observed here.
 - FINDING: `TestModelCheckProductionEntrypoint/deadline_override_terminates_both_owned_process_groups` was introduced after the task head.
